enforcer-mcp (0.3.4) unstable; urgency=low

  * New helper + MCP tool: enforcer-cloud-probe-commands /
    cloud_probe_commands. Zero-payload capability discovery — sends
    each candidate Redis command with no arguments and classifies the
    response as passthrough / unknown / forbidden. Useful for UEF-style
    recon of what a REST proxy (Upstash) actually allowlists. Default
    probe set is Streams-focused (XACK, XACKDEL, XAUTOCLAIM, …) plus
    adjacent CVE-adjacent primitives (DEBUG, SCRIPT, MODULE, PUBSUB).

 -- enforcer-swarm <enforcer@localhost>  Fri, 03 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000

enforcer-mcp (0.3.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Five new first-class MCP tools for cloud OTA (Hermes-callable):
    cloud_status, cloud_pull, cloud_rollback_local, cloud_snapshot,
    cloud_restore. Each is schema-validated and audit-logged, so LLM
    agents can drive fleet updates by prompt instead of shelling out
    through exec_command.
  * New enforcer-cloud-snapshot / enforcer-cloud-restore helpers.
    SCAN-driven full-fidelity dump of every enforcer:mcp:* key to a
    gzipped JSON file (default: /var/lib/enforcer-mcp/snapshots/
    <UTC>.json.gz). Restore is drift-protected — refuses to run if any
    live key differs from the snapshot unless --force is passed. Signal
    + latest pointer are written LAST so mid-flight failures never
    leave the fleet in a torn state.
  * debian/control tidy: systemd moved from Depends to Recommends (so
    the .deb installs cleanly inside NetHunter chroots where systemd
    is held via dpkg-divert), jq moved from an implicit runtime dep to
    Recommends (needed by the enforcer-cloud-* scripts but not the
    daemon), curl explicitly Depends since the OTA scripts require it.

 -- enforcer-swarm <enforcer@localhost>  Fri, 03 Jul 2026 09:30:00 +0000

enforcer-mcp (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Chroot-aware maintainer scripts. postinst / postrm / prerm now
    detect the NetHunter dpkg-divert stub (looking for
    /usr/bin/systemctl.real) in addition to the standard /run/systemd/
    system marker. On a diverted / no-systemd host they skip every
    systemctl call and print a hint pointing the operator at the
    cockpit's Autospawn feature instead.
  * enforcer-mcp-set-bind uses the same detection: on real-systemd
    hosts it does the classic `systemctl restart`; in a chroot it
    finds the running server.py via pgrep and SIGTERM/SIGKILLs it,
    trusting the cockpit's autospawn to relaunch on the next probe
    cycle.
  * New docs/NETHUNTER_TAILSCALE.md — the exact userspace-networking
    recipe for getting Tailscale + MagicDNS working inside the
    chroot. Includes the DNS / nsswitch gotchas and the held-package
    minefield.

 -- enforcer-swarm <enforcer@localhost>  Fri, 03 Jul 2026 08:00:00 +0000

enforcer-mcp (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Fix: default server.host in config.yaml.example flipped from
    "127.0.0.1" to "0.0.0.0". Fresh installs on remote swarm nodes were
    only listening on loopback, so the cockpit's tailnet health probe
    could never reach them — nodes appeared permanently offline. The
    daemon still requires a bearer token so this widened bind is safe
    behind Tailscale ACLs.
  * New helper: enforcer-mcp-set-bind. In-place safe edit of
    /etc/enforcer-mcp/config.yaml (timestamped backup + service
    restart) so existing 0.3.0 nodes can be repaired without a config
    rewrite. Idempotent, supports --show to print current value.
  * Postinst upgrade path now inspects the existing config and prints
    a loud hint if it detects the pre-0.3.1 loopback default.

 -- enforcer-swarm <enforcer@localhost>  Fri, 03 Jul 2026 07:15:00 +0000

enforcer-mcp (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship the enforcer-cloud-{push,pull,rollback,status} scripts for
    Redis-as-registry OTA updates. Cockpit pushes the .deb blob (base64)
    + sha256 meta to Upstash; nodes pull, verify, and dpkg -i without
    needing SCP-per-node. Rollback is one command (swaps latest ↔
    previous keys atomically). See README §Cloud OTA.
  * Scripts auto-source creds from /etc/enforcer-mcp/cloud.env,
    ~/.enforcer-cloud.env, env vars, or --url/--token CLI flags.
  * jq + coreutils base64 are the only new runtime deps (already
    installed on Kali / Debian / NetHunter).

 -- enforcer-swarm <enforcer@localhost>  Fri, 03 Jul 2026 02:00:00 +0000

enforcer-mcp (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add in-app Tier 1 deployment helper: cockpit bundles this .deb as an
    Expo asset, serves it via a Tailscale-bound busybox httpd, and renders
    a copy-pasteable curl|dpkg one-liner for swarm onboarding.
  * Postinst stays idempotent across upgrades — existing /etc/enforcer-mcp/
    config.yaml (and therefore bearer token) is preserved.
  * No code changes vs 0.1.0; version bump exists purely so dpkg -i over a
    deployed 0.1.0 node performs a clean upgrade.

